# Backend stack

| Concern | Owner |
|---|---|
| Runtime / language | Node 22 (`.nvmrc`), TypeScript 5.9 strict, ESM (`"type": "module"`, NodeNext) |
| HTTP | Express 5, `helmet`, `cors`, `express-rate-limit` 8 |
| Validation, config, DTOs | Zod 4 (`config/env.ts`, `schemas/`) |
| Database | PostgreSQL 17, Drizzle ORM 0.45 + `postgres` (postgres.js 3), drizzle-kit migrations |
| Auth | `jose` 6 (HS256 access tokens), `@node-rs/argon2` (argon2id), opaque refresh tokens |
| Logging | `pino` 10 + `pino-http` 11 (`pino-pretty` in dev only) |
| API docs | `@asteasolutions/zod-to-openapi` (OpenAPI 3.1) + `swagger-ui-express` |
| Tests | Vitest 5, `supertest`, `@testcontainers/postgresql` (`postgres:17-alpine`) |
| Lint / format / layers | ESLint 9 + `typescript-eslint` strictTypeChecked, Prettier, dependency-cruiser |

- No second library for an owned concern: no `joi`/`yup`/`class-validator`, no `dotenv` (`process.loadEnvFile`), no `winston`/`morgan`, no `jsonwebtoken`/`bcrypt`, no Prisma/TypeORM/Knex, no Jest, no `axios` (global `fetch` via `createResilientHttpClient`), no DI container library.
- Configuration is read once in `config/env.ts` (`loadEnv()` → typed `Env`). No `process.env.X` anywhere else in `src/`, except `drizzle.config.ts` and the seed's own schema.
- `src/container.ts` is the only composition root: plain `create*` factories, no decorators, no classes for services.
- `src/server.ts` is the only file that listens. `createApp(env, logger, container)` builds the app without listening.
- Before using an API you are not sure of, fetch current docs through the `context7` MCP server.

